---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const faqJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What counts as high heat chilli?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "High heat chilli is 20,000–50,000 Scoville Heat Units (SHU) — strong, lingering heat for hot sauces, snack seasoning and industrial food. Representative varieties are Sanying (Tianying), Zidantou, Seven-Star and New Generation."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is high heat chilli used for?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "High heat chilli is the backbone of hot sauces, chilli oil, snack and instant-noodle seasoning, and industrial food applications that need real, consistent heat."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which variety should I choose for hot sauce?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Sanying (Tianying) and Zidantou are the classic hot-sauce varieties at 20,000–50,000 SHU; Seven-Star is common in snack seasoning and hot-pot bases. Specify the variety and a precise SHU window for batch-to-batch consistency."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="High Heat Chilli (20,000–50,000 SHU) | Tenda Peppers"
  description="High heat chilli (20,000–50,000 SHU) — Sanying, Zidantou and Seven-Star for hot sauce, chilli oil and snack seasoning. China manufacturer, ISO 9001 & HACCP."
  jsonLd={[faqJsonLd]}
>
  <div class="container section">
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="font-size:0.9rem;color:#6b5a54;margin-bottom:16px;">
      <a href="/">Home</a> &rsaquo; <a href="/products/dried-chillies/">Dried Chillies</a> &rsaquo; High Heat
    </nav>
    <h1>High Heat Chilli (20,000–50,000 SHU)</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Strong, lingering heat — the 20,000–50,000 SHU band powers hot sauces, chilli oil and snack
      seasoning, built on varieties like Sanying (Tianying), Zidantou and Seven-Star.
    </p>

    <div class="takeaways">
      <strong>Short answer:</strong> High heat is the 20,000–50,000 SHU band — the sweet spot for hot sauce, chilli oil and snack seasoning where heat is a defining feature but not the only point. Sanying, Zidantou and Seven-Star are the workhorse varieties in this band.
    </div>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">What counts as high heat chilli?</h2>
    <p>
      High heat is the band where chilli stops being a background note and becomes the point of the
      product. It spans 20,000–50,000 SHU — hot enough for dedicated hot-sauce and snack applications,
      but still controllable in a blend when dosed by weight.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Variety</th><th>Heat (SHU)</th><th>Region</th><th>Best for</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Sanying / Tianying</strong></td><td>20,000 – 50,000</td><td>Henan, Hebei</td><td>Hot sauce, chilli oil</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Zidantou (bullet pepper)</strong></td><td>20,000 – 50,000</td><td>Shandong, Anhui</td><td>Hot sauce, industrial food</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Seven-Star</strong></td><td>20,000 – 50,000</td><td>Shandong, Shanxi</td><td>Snack seasoning, hot-pot</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>New Generation</strong></td><td>20,000 – 50,000</td><td>Shandong</td><td>Seasoning, powder</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">What is high heat chilli used for?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Hot sauces and chilli oil</li>
      <li>Snack and instant-noodle seasoning</li>
      <li>Hot-pot and Sichuan-style bases</li>
      <li>Industrial food and processed seasoning</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">How to specify high heat chilli</h2>
    <p>
      Start from your target SHU window, then name the variety. Sanying and Zidantou are the classic
      hot-sauce pair; Seven-Star suits snack and hot-pot bases. Confirm form (powder, flakes or
      segments), moisture and mesh — heat is non-linear, so a precise window is what keeps your sauce
      consistent batch to batch.
    </p>
    <p class="data-note">
      Heat values are representative per variety. Confirm your exact SHU window and form when you
      inquire.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>What counts as high heat chilli?</h3>
      <p>High heat chilli is 20,000–50,000 Scoville Heat Units (SHU) — strong, lingering heat for hot sauces, snack seasoning and industrial food. Representative varieties are Sanying (Tianying), Zidantou, Seven-Star and New Generation.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>What is high heat chilli used for?</h3>
      <p>High heat chilli is the backbone of hot sauces, chilli oil, snack and instant-noodle seasoning, and industrial food applications that need real, consistent heat.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>Which variety should I choose for hot sauce?</h3>
      <p>Sanying (Tianying) and Zidantou are the classic hot-sauce varieties at 20,000–50,000 SHU; Seven-Star is common in snack seasoning and hot-pot bases. Specify the variety and a precise SHU window for batch-to-batch consistency.</p>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top:32px;">
      <a class="cta" href="/contact/">Request High Heat Quotation</a>
      <a class="cta cta-outline" href="/heat-levels/extra-hot/" style="margin-left:8px;">Extra Hot →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
